  "situation": "Four sins against the Spirit, and each is a different verb from a different book. *Quench* is 1 Thessalonians v. 19 · *strive against* is Stephen's *ye do always resist the Holy Ghost*, Acts vii. 51 · *grieve* is Ephesians iv. 30 · *do despite* is Hebrews x. 29, *hath done despite unto the Spirit of grace*. A reader with only the English will hear a rhetorical heap where the plate has four distinct scriptural offences, gathered from four books and set in ascending order of gravity. None is a synonym for another.",
